    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1102">

                <pb facs="0802" n="686" xml:id="pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/1375.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Simpich to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is respectfully suggested that authority be granted to advise Americans who
                    insist on returning to Mexico against Consul’s advice that should they be
                    obliged soon to leave Mexico again and find themselves destitute at the border
                    that they should not expect Government aid in reaching their homes in the
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simpich</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
